SDL2 runtime - /system/lib/libsdl2.swo
========================================

The SDL2-compatible graphics/input runtime is a REAL FILE on the system
volume, at /system/lib/libsdl2.swo. Applications do not carry SDL code
inside their binaries; they map this file at runtime.

Why
---
Philosophy rule 1 (/system/doc/philosophy.txt): EVERYTHING IS A REAL
FILE ON A REAL DISK. A library baked into every app binary would be a
hidden copy - undeletable, unlistable, unreplaceable, and invisible to
the file manager. libsdl2.swo is the single copy: you can list it in
Files, checksum it, replace it with a rebuild, or delete it and watch
every SDL app fail with a clear "cannot load /system/lib/libsdl2.swo"
instead of pretending nothing happened.

File format
-----------
A standard ELF64 shared object (ET_DYN), linked at vaddr 0:

  - position independent,
  - self-contained: NO undefined symbols (the freestanding formatter,
    mem/str helpers and allocator forwarding live inside, in
    sdl_libc.c),
  - .rela.dyn contains R_X86_64_RELATIVE entries ONLY (a version
    script exports just the entry symbol, so internal calls bind at
    link time),
  - e_entry points at one function:

        const SDL2_Api *sdl2_api_get(const SDL2_Hooks *hooks);

    It receives the consumer's allocator and returns the relocated API
    table (user/lib/sdl2/sdl2_api.h is the contract).

How apps load it
----------------
Apps link the tiny loader stub user/lib/sdl2_dyn.c (~200 lines of
forwarders) and call, before any other SDL call:

    sdl2_open(0);        /* NULL = /system/lib/libsdl2.swo */

which does:
  1. SYS_LIB_LOAD(76) -> kernel/dynlib.c maps the file resident (LIB
     pool, pages tagged PMMO_LIB) and applies the relocations,
  2. reads e_entry from the same file (the file is the contract),
  3. calls it with {malloc, free, calloc, realloc} from the app's own
     allocator (sdl_heap.o for plain apps, the doomcompat allocator
     for DOOM),
  4. stores the returned table; every SDL_* forwarder goes through it
     - the same pattern as SDL's own dynapi.

Consumers on this volume
------------------------
  /system/apps/doom.elf      DOOM (doomgeneric_sdl backend)
  /system/apps/sdltest.elf   video smoke test (surface + renderer)
  /system/apps/sdlin.elf     input smoke test (keys/mouse/close)
  /system/apps/gametest.elf  gamelib + IMG + renderer self-test (GAMETEST: ALL PASS)
