Kernel side: /system/doc/syscall-abi.txt addendum v2, syscall 76.
Source: user/lib/sdl2/ (the library) and user/lib/sdl2_dyn.c (stub).

What is implemented (r15)
-------------------------
  video     windows (one WM window each; OpenGL windows: see OPENGL below), window surface, surfaces
            (blit/stretch/fill/colorkey/alpha+color mod, BMP load/save)
  render    software renderer: blend NONE/BLEND/ADD/MOD/MUL, points/lines/
            rects (int + float), RenderCopy/CopyEx/CopyF/CopyExF (scale, flip,
            rotation about any pivot, nearest or bilinear), logical size,
            SetScale, viewport, clip, render targets, streaming textures,
            ReadPixels. Textures are ARGB8888 internally.
            Like real SDL2, SDL_RenderClear ignores viewport and clip rect.
  events    keyboard (scancodes/keycodes/mods/state), mouse, window events,
            text input, SDL_PushEvent/PeepEvents, user events
  timers    SDL_AddTimer (run from PumpEvents/Delay - single threaded)
  files     RWops (file + memory), SDL_LoadFile, GetBasePath/GetPrefPath
  audio     NULL device only: callbacks run at real time, output is discarded
            (SwirlOS has no sound-card driver yet). Games run, silently.
  threads   NOT supported: SDL_CreateThread fails with an error, mutexes and
            semaphores are single-threaded stubs.
  not here  GLES, shaders, SDL_ttf, SDL_mixer, joysticks/game controllers.
            SDL_image-style loading is provided app-side by gameimg.h.

Self-test
---------
Set  [test] sdl = gametest  in /system/config/swirl.conf and boot: the serial
log ends with "GAMETEST: ALL PASS" (or "GAMETEST: n FAILED" + the failing
check). Use sdltest / sdlin for the original video / input smoke tests.

OPENGL (SDL_GL_*, r15)
----------------------
SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL windows + SDL_GL_* are implemented. The GL itself is TinyGL
(software OpenGL 1.1, fixed function) built INTO libsdl2.swo; a game links
build/sdlapp/sdl2_gl_dyn.o (gl* forwarders, resolved once through
SDL_GL_GetProcAddress) and includes <SDL2/SDL_opengl.h> (or <GL/gl.h>).

  SDL_GL_CreateContext / DeleteContext / MakeCurrent / SwapWindow
  SDL_GL_SetSwapInterval (0 = free run, 1 = ~60 Hz)  SDL_GL_Get/SetAttribute
  SDL_GL_GetProcAddress  SDL_GL_GetDrawableSize  SDL_GL_Get/ResetAttributes
  SDL_GL_ExtensionSupported (always false)  SDL_GL_LoadLibrary (no-op)

Rendering goes straight into the WM's tear-free flip buffers (no copy); the
window cannot also use SDL_GetWindowSurface / SDL_Renderer.

Limits (read before porting a game):
  - ONE context at a time, GL 1.1 fixed function only. No shaders, no VBOs,
    no FBOs, no GL_EXT/ARB extensions. Display lists, vertex arrays
    (FLOAT/DOUBLE/INT/SHORT/BYTE element types, byte strides),
    lighting, fog calls (ignored), glOrtho/glFrustum, glReadPixels work.
  - Textures: every glTexImage2D image (RGB/RGBA/BGR/BGRA/LUMINANCE/ALPHA/
    LUMINANCE_ALPHA, UNSIGNED_BYTE, any size) is resampled to 256x256 and
    sampled NEAREST + REPEAT. Mip levels > 0 are ignored. 256 KB of heap per
    texture: the SDL app heap is 3 MB, budget for it.
  - NO blending. glEnable(GL_BLEND or GL_ALPHA_TEST) turns on 1-bit alpha
    KEYING for textures (texel alpha >= 128 is drawn, the rest skipped), which
    covers sprites/fonts/foliage but not translucency. glBlendFunc,
    glDepthFunc/Mask, glAlphaFunc, glScissor, glColorMask, glPointSize,
    glLineWidth, glFog* are accepted and ignored.
  - 16-bit depth buffer, LEQUAL-style test, window width rounded down to a
    multiple of 4. glTexSubImage2D is not supported (GL_INVALID_OPERATION).
  - TinyGL never terminates the process: unsupported parameters set a GL
    error (glGetError) and the call is dropped.
